DESCRIPTION:The Montclair Foundation & Studio Players Announce an Immersive Production of Much Ado About Nothing Set for a July 2026 Debut \nGet ready for a Shakespearean takeover! The Montclair Foundation/Van Vleck House & Gardens and Studio Players are delighted to present William Shakespeare’s classic comedy of romance and intrigue\, “Much Ado About Nothing\,” opening July 10. This is no ordinary stage production; it’s an immersive theatrical experience. The grounds will be completely transformed into the site of a comedy of errors. Audience members will find themselves in the heart of the action as Shakespearean actors bring the story to life throughout the gardens \nMuch Ado About Nothing 360° \nThe play\, originally set in and around a castle in 16th Century Messina\, Italy\, is structurally ideal for the Van Vleck location as it moves from lush interiors to cultivated exteriors\, and the staging will create an immersive opportunity for attendees to explore the beauty of the Van Vleck estate while simultaneously enjoying one of the Bard’s most beloved comedies. Studio Players will begin casting the production in mid-March. \nPerformances will be held on July 10th – 11th and July 17th- 18th from 7:00 PM – 8:00 PM\, with rain dates to be announced. Join us for a VIP Opening Night celebration on Friday\, July 10th at 6:00 PM\, featuring a lively pre-show reception with champagne and hors d’oeuvres to kick off the production in style. Opening Night tickets are $75\, while general admission tickets for all other performances are $50. Tickets are available at the link below or by contacting the box office at (973) 744-9752. \n \n  \nAbout the Play \nOriginally penned in 1598-1599\, Much Ado About Nothing is a rollicking comedy centered around two romantic couples\, the naive and wistful Claudio and Hero\, and the more worldly-wise Benedick and Beatrice. Situated in and around a medieval castle in Messina\, Sicily\, the story unfolds as members of Don Pedro’s army de